# ============================================================================
# 05_ WGCNA module detection + ASPC/NEPC module-trait association — v2
# ============================================================================
# Consumes the bulk cohort plus the single-cell feature evidence from 02_/03_,
# and writes the module-membership table that 06_ integrates.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE MAIN DEFECT IN v1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1 residualised expression on ASPC_fraction:
#
#     cov_use <- cov_tbl %>% select(any_of(c("purity", "ASPC_fraction",
#                                            "immune_fraction", "stromal_fraction")))
#
# That regresses the ASPC signal OUT of the matrix before module detection.
# Any co-expression module driven by adipose stem/progenitor content is
# removed by construction, and the modules that survive cannot be ASPC
# modules. Since 06_ uses `in_wgcna_module` as evidence that a gene belongs
# to an ASPC-associated programme, v1's flag could not carry that meaning.
#
# v2 excludes ASPC_fraction from residualisation, matching the decision
# already taken in 04_ ("do NOT residualize on ASPC_fraction because it is a
# target"). Technical covariates — purity, immune, stromal — are still
# removed. cfg$resid_covariates makes this explicit and auditable.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SECOND DEFECT: no module-trait step
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1 flagged `in_wgcna_module` for ANY gene in ANY non-grey module with
# |kME| >= 0.30 — roughly half the genes in a typical run. That is not
# evidence of ASPC association; it is evidence of being co-expressed with
# something.
#
# v2 adds the missing step: correlate every module eigengene with
# ASPC_fraction and with NEPC_score, identify the ASPC-associated module(s)
# by FDR-corrected correlation, and set `in_wgcna_module` TRUE only for genes
# in those modules. The permissive v1 definition is retained alongside as
# `in_any_module` so nothing is silently lost.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OTHER CHANGES IN v2
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   * Paths corrected to /Volumes/Jingjing_Chen (v1 used "Jingjing Chen").
#   * NEPC_score computed identically to 04_ (same signature, same z-scaling)
#     so the two scripts agree on the trait.
#   * Residualisation vectorised: one qr.resid() solve replaces a 10,000-
#     iteration lm.fit loop.
#   * kME lookup vectorised via matrix indexing; v1 did a linear scan of
#     kME_df per gene (O(n^2) — minutes on 10k genes).
#   * Membership table annotated with tau (02_) and ratio (03_) so 06_ can
#     see all three lines of evidence in one place.
#   * Module-trait heatmap, eigengene table, and module summary written out.
#   * out_dir is date-stamped automatically rather than hard-coded.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OUTPUTS (out_dir)
#   wgcna_module_membership.csv   gene, module, kME, in_wgcna_module   <- 06_
#   wgcna_module_trait.csv        module x trait correlation + FDR
#   wgcna_module_summary.csv      per-module size, ASPC r, NEPC r, verdict
#   wgcna_eigengenes.csv          sample x module eigengene values
#   wgcna_result.rds              datExpr, MEs, colours, params
#   wgcna.PROVENANCE.txt
#   *.pdf                         QC, soft threshold, dendrogram, trait heatmap
# ============================================================================

